<title>USA: U.S. mortgage refinancing volume up 9.8 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. mortgage refinancing volume up 9.8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The volume of U.S. mortgage refinancing applications jumped 9.8 percent in the week ended July 25, according to a Mortgage Bankers Association of America weekly survey.</p>
<p>The total volume of mortgage applications gained 2.3 percent in the latest survey week, while applications to purchase mortgages dropped 0.8 percent.</p>
<p>The seasonally adjusted refinancing index rose 9.8 percent to 595.9 from 542.8 percent the previous week. The purchase index dipped 1.2 percent to 205.9 in the latest survey from 208.4 in the previous week.  </p>
